## Success Criteria

### Immediate (Week 1)
- ✅ All 8 current rabbit holes closed or properly archived
- ✅ Daily Briefing delivered at 8 AM
- ✅ User reports "mental load reduced"

### Systemic (Week 2)
- ✅ Commitment ledger auto-populates from artifacts
- ✅ Aging detection catches commitments >7 days
- ✅ Nightly digest shows 0 red-tier items
- ✅ Quick Close workflow tested and approved
- ✅ Context-aware routing working (tests novelty/dopamine dimensions)
- ✅ Pattern templates created for 4 commitment types
- ✅ Coordination metrics dashboard showing in Satellite View

### Personal (Week 4)
- ✅ Week 1 challenge completed
- ✅ User reports "easier to do external work"
- ✅ Open rabbit holes <2 sustained for 7+ days
- ✅ Guilt-free operation for 14+ days
- ✅ Auto-closure rate >30% (system learning your patterns)
- ✅ Coordination efficiency improving week-over-week

---

## Risk Mitigation

| Risk | Mitigation |
|:-----|:-----------|
| User overwhelmed by briefings | Start with 1 briefing/day, adjust frequency |
| Auto-detection misses commitments | Manual "log commitment" command as fallback |
| Closure options don't fit | Add "custom" option with free text |
| Telegram delivery fails | Graceful degradation: Email → SMS → File backup |
| User ignores briefings | Gamification, progress visualization |
| Context-aware routing mis-classifies | Track misses, adjust weighting |
| Template library doesn't match | Allow custom templates, learn from usage |

